Altar Server Handbook

Welcome to the altar server ministry at St. Columba. Servers assist at weekend Masses, funerals and holy days.

Who may serve: Altar servers must have received First Communion and be in at least fourth grade.

Training is held twice a year, in September and in January, in the church. New servers shadow an experienced server for three Masses.

Servers arrive 20 minutes before Mass, vest in the sacristy and check the credence table.

Schedules are posted monthly. If you cannot serve, find a substitute from the server list and tell the sacristan.

Dress: dark shoes and dark pants or skirt under the alb.
